      "id": "Xref",
      "code_hash": "0130f900a482fad05f7b5b80d0c5a634",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"calculate-the-counterterm-insertions\">Calculate the counterterm insertions</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The one-loop result supplies <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_\\psi=-\\xi/\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex> and the Ward\nrelation <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_1=\\delta Z_\\psi||)</marimo-tex>. Insert it once at each of the two\nvertices, and once on each of the two fermion lines. A kinetic insertion\nmultiplies the numerator by <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(-\\delta Z_\\psi q_e^2||)</marimo-tex> and squares that\nfermion denominator. Shared UV expansion and one-loop IBP calculate all\nfour contributions; the finite tadpole term is needed because each\ninsertion already contains <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(1/\\epsilon||)</marimo-tex>.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">These are explicitly constructed local insertions on a generated graph.\nThis example does not enumerate arbitrary counterterm models or forests.\nThe one-loop bubble also determines <marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_{A,1}||)</marimo-tex> and the auxiliary\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(\\delta Z_{Am,1}||)</marimo-tex>. The reference's auxiliary operator is\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(iM(Z_{Am}^2-1)g^{\\mu\\nu}||)</marimo-tex>, so its two-loop term includes\n<marimo-tex class=\"arithmatex\">||(2\\delta Z_{Am,2}+\\delta Z_{Am,1}^2||)</marimo-tex>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "SFPL",
